<title>PARAGUAY: Paraguay to set up anti-forgery council - radio.</title>
<headline>Paraguay to set up anti-forgery council - radio.</headline>
<dateline>ASUNCION 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paraguay's government will create a watchdog to crack down on copyright violations, local radio reported Tuesday.</p>
<p>The National Copyright Protection Council will begin to operate in two months and will include representatives from the ministries of Justice, Trade and Industry, Education and Finance.</p>
<p>The council will fight audio and video pirating and forged brand products.</p>
<p>The U.S. Commerce Department in 1995 included Paraguay in a list of countries under observation for forgery industries.</p>
<p>-- Asuncion Newsroom +59521 44-4527</p>
</text>
